          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "Net-(R34-Pad2) : R34.2(2,passive) SW6.1(passive)"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "Net-(R35-Pad2) : R35.2(2,passive) SW6.2(passive)"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "/CAN0_P : ... SW6.4(passive)"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "/CAN1_P : ... SW6.3(passive)"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "Closing the DIP switch shorts the two isolated CAN buses together, defeating isolation and causing bus contention. Termination is not correctly applied.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "category": "open_connection",
      "components": ["D14", "D23", "D4"],
      "pins": ["D14.2", "D23.2", "D4.2"],
      "nets": ["/LED_3.3V_POWER_SW"],
      "observed": "Net /LED_3.3V_POWER_SW contains only the anodes of D14, D23, and D4. It has no connection to any power source or driver.",
      "expected": "The anodes of these LEDs should be connected to a 3.3V power source (e.g., +3V3) or a switched 3.3V rail, so that the LEDs can be illuminated when their cathodes are pulled low.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "/LED_3.3V_POWER_SW : D14.2(A,passive) D23.2(A,passive) D4.2(A,passive)"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "D14, D23, and D4 (Ethernet and activity LEDs) will never light because their anodes are floating.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The design files contain multiple anomalies: USB-C VBUS is shorted to D-, the CAN termination DIP switch cross-wires the two isolated CAN buses, and the anodes of three status LEDs are left floating. These deviations would prevent proper USB communication, defeat CAN isolation, and disable status LEDs."
}

